# The build context is the whole repository, because the image needs the backend,
# the frontend and the delivered CSVs. Everything below is either rebuilt inside the
# image or would invalidate its layer cache on every change.

# Version control and agent tooling: never in a runtime image.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.opencode
.agents
.scratch
skills-lock.json
AGENTS.md
CONTEXT.md
Prueba_Tecnica_AI_Energy_Management.docx (1).md
Prueba_Tecnica_AI_Energy_Management.docx (1).pdf
*.md
!data/*.md

# Dependencies are installed inside the image against the lockfiles, so a host
# node_modules would only shadow them with a different platform's build.
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist

# Go's build cache and the binaries a host build leaves behind.
backend/bin
backend/data
backend/.env
